commit d9166333616f4575749e64873796ad6a96f01c93
Author: Colin Watson <cjwatson@debian.org>
Date:   Tue Sep 1 01:14:44 2026 +0100

    Don't link sshd against libselinux
    
    When configured with --with-selinux, the main sshd binary only appears
    to need symbols from libselinux because functions that it needs are in
    the same translation units as functions that use libselinux, meaning
    that `ld --as-needed` doesn't realize that it can drop those functions
    and the resulting DT_NEEDED tag.
    
    This should have the effect of dropping libselinux and libpcre2-8 from
    sshd's linkage in the configuration used by several common Linux
    distributions, including Debian.

